Within instance w of model Scope in Study, consider only connect equations written directly in Scope (not connect equations declared within component classes). Determine the canonical signed coefficient vector for the primitive flow connection set containing w.deep.left.a.f. Include every member of that scope-local set, sort paths lexicographically, reduce any global common factor, and orient the vector so the first coefficient is positive. Return the answer as comma-separated path:coefficient pairs.

Modelica source:
```modelica
connector T08
  Real v;
  flow Real f;
end T08;

connector T21
  T08 a;
end T21;

connector T04
  T08 a;
  T08 b;
end T04;

connector T17
  T21 branch;
end T17;

connector T10
  T21 left;
  T21 right;
end T10;

model T03
  T08 a;
  Real x;
equation
  a.v = x;
  a.f = x;
end T03;

model T15
  T08 a;
  T08 b;
  Real xa;
  Real xb;
equation
  a.v = xa;
  a.f = xa;
  b.v = xb;
  b.f = xb;
end T15;

model T06
  T21 branch;
  Real x;
equation
  branch.a.v = x;
  branch.a.f = x;
end T06;

model T19
  T21 left;
  T21 right;
  Real xleft;
  Real xright;
equation
  left.a.v = xleft;
  left.a.f = xleft;
  right.a.v = xright;
  right.a.f = xright;
end T19;

model T12
  T08 p;
  Real x;
equation
  p.v = x;
  p.f = x;
end T12;

model T01
  T08 port;
  T12 core;
equation
  connect(port, core.p);
end T01;

model Scope
  T10 deep;
  T21 side;
  T12 load;
equation
  connect(deep.left.a, side.a);
  connect(side.a, load.p);
  connect(load.p, deep.right.a);
end Scope;

model Study
  Scope w;
end Study;
```

